Green: **625 total, 625 passing, 0 failing** (exit 0).

The fix — one line in `src/pricing.js:39`:

```js
function orderTotal(cents, discountPct, taxRate) {
  const discounted = applyDiscount(cents, discountPct);
  return applyTax(discounted, taxRate);
}
```

Tax now applies to the discounted amount, which matches the spec in `cases.js:89` and the function's own doc comment. Nothing else in the suite was actually broken — the other 622 cases were passing all along, just drowned in the verbose output.

One note worth flagging: the old code over-charged tax on every order that had both a discount and a nonzero tax rate. If this engine has been billing real orders, those charges were too high (e.g. the 33400c / 10% / 20% row: 42345c charged vs 36072c owed). Might be worth checking whether any of that reached production.
